{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This structure represents approximately 30-40% of a complete D96A EANCOM INVOIC ontology. While the foundational envelope/message/segment architecture is present, critical transactional segments (monetary amounts, tax details, dates, quantities, references, allowances/charges) are entirely absent. The current model cannot validate a real invoice without 12-15 additional segment types and their business rule constraints.",

  "completeness_score": 0.35,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "MOA_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Monetary Amount segment is MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC. Required at header level (total invoice amount with qualifier 79) and line level (line amounts with qualifier 203). Without this, no financial validation is possible."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Date/Time segment", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 4}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "The revised structure shows significant improvement with 24 classes and 28 properties, covering foundational invoice architecture. However, critical D96A INVOIC segments remain absent. A complete EANCOM INVOIC ontology requires ~18-22 segment types; you have modeled only 4 explicit segments (BGM, NAD, MOA, DTM). Missing high-priority elements include line item details (LIN, PIA, QTY, PRI), tax structures (TAX), references (RFF), allowances/charges (ALC), and packaging (PAC).",

  "completeness_score": 0.45,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "LIN_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Line Item segment is MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC. Without LIN, you cannot represent individual invoice lines. Must include line number (C212/7140) and item identification."
    },
    {
      "type": "class", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 3}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "The ontology now demonstrates strong structural coverage of D96A INVOIC core segments (~75-80% segment coverage). However, critical semantic gaps remain: missing UNS (section control), incomplete composite element modeling (C516 for MOA, C507 for DTM), absent code list constraints, and no cardinality enforcement axioms. The model is architecturally sound but semantically incomplete for production validation.",

  "completeness_score": 0.72,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "UNS_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "The UNS (Section Control) segment is MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC to separate header/detail from summary sections. Without it, parsers cannot distinguish between line-level MOA and message-level MOA. This is a structural requirement, not optional."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "C516_MonetaryAmount",
      "priority": "high", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 2}

{"expert_response": "```json
