{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling but exhibits critical D96A EANCOM INVOIC compliance failures. The primary issues are: (1) Complete absence of qualifier-based segment distinctions (NAD+BY vs NAD+SU are conflated), (2) Missing ~40% of mandatory D96A segments, (3) No cardinality constraints enforcing EANCOM business rules, (4) Data type constraints are entirely absent (GLN n13 validation impossible).",
  "completeness_score": 0.58,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "NAD_Buyer_Segment (NAD+BY)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A EANCOM mandates distinct modeling of NAD segments by qualifier. The current generic NAD_Segment class cannot enforce that Buyer identification (GLN mandatory) differs from Supplier (GLN + VAT mandatory). This is a semantic flattening error - all party roles are indistinguishable."", "owl_reviewed_length": 34807, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

