{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates strong OWL modeling practices with comprehensive inverse properties and disjointness axioms, but it critically fails to capture the EDIFACT D96A INVOIC standard. It models generic invoice concepts rather than the specific segment-based structure mandated by EANCOM. The ontology is missing ~70% of required D96A INVOIC segments and lacks qualifier-based semantic distinctions that are fundamental to EDIFACT.",
  "completeness_score": 0.25,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTMSegment with qualifier-based subclasses (DTM+137, DTM+35, DTM+11, etc.)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Date/Time segments are MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC. DTM+137 (Document Date) is required in header. The current model has only a generic 'hasDocumentDate' datatype property, which loses the EDIFACT segment structure and qualifier semantics. Must create DTM", "owl_reviewed_length": 21513, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

